# ESP32-Sense-Kit mainboard — ESP32-WROOM-32 module, no PSRAM.
#
# Module CONFIRMED from the schematic (SCH_ESP32-Sense-Series-MainBoard.pdf,
# sheet 1): the ESP32 MODULE block is designator U8, value ESP-WROOM-32, on the
# 39-pin footprint. Corroborated by how the board uses it — sheet 2's IO
# Configure Table routes IO16 to HEADER12 and IO17 to HEADER11, and GPIO16/17
# are consumed internally by the PSRAM on every WROVER, so a WROVER cannot be
# fitted. Hence no CONFIG_SPIRAM.
#
# Flash size 4 MB CONFIRMED. The usual "a schematic names the module, not its
# SKU suffix" caveat does not bite here: the value on U8 is the bare part
# number ESP-WROOM-32, and the ESP32-WROOM-32 datasheet (v3.7) §1.2 Ordering
# Information is a ONE-ROW table — part number ESP32-WROOM-32, flash 4 MB — with
# §1 stating flatly "The module features a 4 MB external SPI flash". The
# multi-size options (4 / 8 / 16 MB) belong to -32D / -32U / -32E, which are
# different part numbers and are not what this sheet fits.
CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_240=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_DIO=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHFREQ_40M=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_4MB=y
